/*
:name: vector_io_ports_bare_type
:type: error
:error: a tuple-type entry must be named
*/
// A tuple TYPE is all-named (`v:(a:U4, b:U8)`) or all-anonymous
// (`v:(_:U4, _:U8)`); a bare type entry such as `U4` is neither, so it is a
// compile error (it used to be silently dropped, leaving a port with no leaves).
// The positional spellings that ARE legal are in pyrope/vector_io_ports.prp.
pub comb vector_io(v:(U4, U8)) -> (o:U12) {  // locate_error_here
  o = v[0] + v[1]
}
